+# Q-0019 combinatorial-compression audit — 2026-08-08
+
+## Purpose
+
+The supplied conversations explored many increasingly specific descriptions of
+the one-coordinate/high-overlap residual.  This audit separates **real
+combinatorial compression** from relabelling.  It is intentionally broader than
+the current normal-zipper route so that useful negative information is not lost.
+
+A step counts as a genuine compression only if it demonstrably reduces at
+least one of:
+
+1. the number of free source coordinates/states;
+2. the arity or sustainable branching of the genealogy;
+3. an actual resource controlled by degree/codegree/support capacity;
+4. a source-owned monotone or telescoping potential.
+
+A smaller name for the residual is not a compression.
+
+## Result ledger
+
+| Conversation result | Disposition | Reason / retained lesson |
+|---|---|---|
+| Output-edge `b^{-2}`/`b^{-3}` fibers | **retain, but source gap remains** | Genuine local codimension; does not control the original fork row. |
+| Specialized hole graph / clique-chain / class-star descriptions | **diagnostic only** | They isolate high-overlap as repeated resampling, but without a source capacity they do not shrink mass. |
+| Missing-square / first-anchor-loss / increasingly fine migration taxonomy | **stop as main activity** | Useful for counterexamples, but later analysis showed further subtype names do not alter the quantitative obligation. |
+| Common-parent parallel singleton repairs | **retain as real compression** | Removes sequential private-witness reset. |
+| Inclusion-minimal bad set has size `2` or `3` | **retain as real compression** | Direct 3-uniform dimensional reduction. |
+| Minimal triple third coordinate gives free `1/b` | **refuted** | Source-owned is not the same as irreversible; the coordinate can be retried. |
+| Parallel rollback | **retain as real compression** | Exactly removes a whole branch and its private deletion trace; closes support synchronization. |
+| Rollback `4 -> 2` gives `b^{-2}` | **refuted** | The rolled-back block may be sampled again. |
+| Protected level alone is globally monotone | **conditional / incomplete** | Two-protected blockers force either deletion of protected endpoints or an independently paid exit. |
+| Protected-pair coverage implies high degree | **refuted** | Degree-one tree example covers an entire hole block. |
+| Pair-state low/high split | **retain as real compression** | Low grammar has exact polynomial `(1+Delta z)^2` and growth `4 Delta`; only high nodes need extra control. |
+| Retained/frozen pair child gives new mark | **refuted as double counting** | The child is already an input obligation. |
+| Three-safe-pegs / safe quadruple | **retain as local gadget only** | Produces real external coordinates and protected stopping shapes, but cross-macro handoff was not proved and cannot itself supply the source mark. |
+| First-use token deletion through the main matching edge | **retain conditionally** | Decoder-safe because the deleting actual edge is already in the record. |
+| Fixed `O(1)` token births per high node close the threshold | **refuted quantitatively** | Near `Delta=b^2/4`, the factor tends to a nonzero constant `2^{-t}` rather than `o(1)`. |
+| Fixed support implies fixed pair | **refuted** | Staircase-style migration and later endpoint computation show the pair may move within one support. |
+| Transition-forest rank gives global unit capacity | **refuted** | The same bare transition can reappear across supports/contexts. |
+| Fresh Shannon/Renyi information telescopes automatically | **refuted** | Each reset may introduce a new random source; no source-owned conservation law was established. |
+| Binary `Q4`: 272 matchings, 8 normal | **retain bounded normal form** | Complete finite obstruction-space compression. |
+| `C/S/R = 192/384/192`, splice uses all 8 edges | **retain bounded normal form** | Existing repository fact, strengthened by unique zipper geometry. |
+| Ternary normal-box density `<=16/81`, extremal center-star | **provisional conversation result** | Reported as exact MILP in the supplied conversation but its generator/certificate is not present in this patch; do not promote until reconstructed. |
+| `16/81` normal density itself contracts source mass | **refuted** | A rooted diagonal codebook can evade the desired rooted cylinder interpretation. |
+| Nonnormal `Q4` has cancellable faces / rooted diagonal exceptions | **provisional conversation result** | Strong bounded structure reported in the supplied conversation; preserve as a reconstruction target, not a canonical fact without its generator. |
+| Rooted-bad edge profile `(1,3,3,1)` and `3B <= 4 Delta (b-1)^2` | **provisional conversation result** | Potentially valuable degree-based incidence inequality; generator/certificate must be restored before promotion. |
+| Normal shared-`q` switching square | **retain observed** | Exhaustive current generator: retain/retain=`C`, mixed=`S`, release/release=`R`. |
+| Normal splice has one eight-edge bridge with seven cuts | **retain observed** | Gives a canonical finite connector rather than seven unrelated witnesses. |
+| Zipper state confluence implies `P^2 -> P` | **refuted as a logical shortcut** | Same state does not imply identical owner/root/stack/provenance future. |
+| Endpoint tuple `(e_1,e_2;q)` is source-static | **refuted by exhaustive computation** | It moves to the opposite bridge seam; endpoint edges are disjoint and `q` changes. |
+| Eight-edge normal support is invariant under the antipodal zipper | **retain observed** | Correct finite invariant inside one binary window. |
+| Eight normal supports form `K4,4` under overlap-2 | **retain observed** | Gives a genuine fixed-window support-packing bound of 4. |
+| `[3]^4` embedded normal supports have packing number 12 | **retain bounded computer-assisted fact** | 648-support transitive family; 12 feasible and 13 infeasible by exact finite MILP. |
+| `(e_1,e_2;q;f_1,f_2)` is codimension one | **retain observed/formal completion count** | Exposes 7 of 8 binary vertices; leaves one `b`-ary complementary value. |
+| The remaining value automatically gives `1/b` | **not proved** | Must be source-owned or exposed by an already-paid faithful event. |
+
+## Superseded intermediate frontiers
+
+Several frontiers were useful because they exposed the next failure, but should
+not remain as the current target:
+
+1. **persistent-anchor extraction from one local heavy coordinate** — too
+   strong; local heavy objects migrate;
+2. **global irreversible peg** — stronger than necessary and not established;
+3. **protected-handoff geometric contraction** — analytically attractive, but
+   state semantics and child double counting were unresolved;
+4. **support synchronization along a cylinder** — superseded by exact parallel
+   rollback;
+5. **strict endpoint persistence** — directly false in normal Q4;
+6. **instantaneous `P^2 -> P` from a splice** — stronger than what confluence
+   proves.
+
+The current useful weakening is: finitely many source-static normal supports
+may be consumed for free; subsequent return must force actual-edge reuse or an
+exact future merge.
+
+## Results from the supplied older proof-gap conversation that remain design constraints
+
+The older conversation repeatedly arrived at the same meta-obstruction through
+different local graphs, switch planes, and entropy variables: a local
+high-overlap residual can be described very finely without reducing source
+mass.  The following conclusions remain valuable even where the intermediate
+notation has been retired:
+
+- the high-overlap regime is essentially repeated one-coordinate/pair reuse,
+  not a failure of the local `b^{-2}` output count;
+- a full two-dimensional switch plane is more informative than following one
+  reset path, but it must be tied to source ownership before producing a charge;
+- a finite transition graph or potential is an organizer, not an automatic
+  degree bound;
+- new entropy at every restart is not a telescoping source budget;
+- any proposed `o(1)` high mark must be checked against the actual pair record
+  language to exclude charging an already-existing child;
+- after all descriptive reductions, progress must come from actual capacity,
+  exact obligation cancellation, or a source-owned return potential.
+
+These principles are now encoded in the Q-0019 route rather than preserved as
+separate migration subtypes.
+
+## Current compression chain
+
+The net chain that survives audit is
+
+\[
+\boxed{
+\begin{aligned}
+\text{arbitrary sequential genealogy}
+&\to\text{common-parent parallel genealogy}\\
+&\to |I|\le3\text{ minimal interaction}\\
+&\to\text{exact branch rollback}\\
+&\to\text{low pair grammar }(1+\Delta z)^2\\
+&\to\text{rank-two high core}\\
+&\to\text{finite normal support / collision frontier}.
+\end{aligned}}
+\]
+
+Every displayed arrow removes a real freedom.  The last line still needs a
+quantitative owner-weighted recurrence; therefore Q-0019 remains open.
